{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Morning. Your screen's still on the login, so I'll read the obs. Blood pressure 148 over 92, pulse 96, temperature 36.8, oxygen sats 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Uhh, it's in. I missed the dip. What did the urine show?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): Urine dip, blood three plus, protein trace, leucocytes negative, nitrites negative, pH 6.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Say that once more? I typed over it.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (NURSE): Blood three plus, protein trace, leucocytes negative, nitrites negative, pH 6.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ta. Mr Brennan. Sorry, the discharge letters had me. What's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Good morning, doctor. I have come because of a sudden severe pain overnight, and blood in my urine.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (DOCTOR): Where is the pain? Slowly again, I had the wrong file open.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): It began in the right loin. I do apologise, that is incorrect. It is the left loin, and it travels down into the left groin.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'm his wife. He was holding the left side, pacing the hall. White as a sheet.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): Left, down to the groin. Sudden?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): Entirely sudden, doctor. It woke me at about two, perhaps a little after two. It has not settled, and it comes in waves.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (DOCTOR): Out of ten? The pain score keeps jumping fields. Umm.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): I would put the left loin pain at seven. When a wave peaks it is nearer eight, and it has been so since about two this morning.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any vomiting?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes, doctor. I vomited once, around three o'clock. I have not vomited since.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): You saw the blood? Say it again, my phone went.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): I did. The urine was pink the first time, and red the next. I saw no clot.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): No, doctor. I have not felt feverish.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any cough?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): No cough at all.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Weight. Have you lost weight? Sorry, yes or no, I clicked the path results.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (PATIENT): I would not say I have lost weight, exactly. My trousers sit a little looser, yet I have not weighed myself, so I cannot be sure.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ever had this sort of pain before?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): I believe I had a milder bout once. It passed after a day or so. As to when, err, I cannot tell you. Last winter, or possibly the winter before. I simply cannot date it.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Medicines, then. The list on screen looks stale. What do you take?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (PATIENT): I take perindapril, five milligrams each morning, for my blood pressure. Forgive me, both parts of that are wrong. The medicine is perindopril, and I take ten milligrams by mouth each morning. The dose was put up.",
  "[SEG0029] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The box on the bench says perindopril ten milligrams. I looked before we left.",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): I also took some paracetamol at home for the pain. Two tablets. No, it was three tablets. They helped very little.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): Allergies? Blank on the screen, and I don't trust a blank.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (PATIENT): No allergies that I am aware of, doctor.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): High blood pressure, ongoing? Say it back while I fix the chart.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): Yes. High blood pressure for some years, still under treatment.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Known hypertension, then. Any operations?",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (PATIENT): An appendicectomy when I was nineteen. Nothing since.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): I have never smoked, doctor.",
  "[SEG0039] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The car park meter took my coins and gave me nothing. Maddening. I know, not why we're here.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. Left loin is tender to palpation. Abdomen is soft with no guarding, and there's no hernia in the groin.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, working impression only, not a firm diagnosis. This fits renal colic from a stone on the left, with the pain into the groin and the blood. The scan still has to confirm it.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): Today I'll book a CT of the urinary tract for this afternoon. For the pain, oxycodone five milligrams by mouth now. I won't use an anti-inflammatory while you're on perindopril and the kidney might be blocked.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (NURSE): I can give that oxycodone before you go, and I'll ring CT for an afternoon slot.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come back to clinic tomorrow morning and we'll go through the result. If you cannot pass urine, or the pain gets away from you, go to emergency rather than waiting.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (PATIENT): Thank you, doctor. I understand. We will return tomorrow morning.",
  "[SEG0046] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We'll keep an eye on him overnight. Thank you for seeing us so quickly."
 ],
